From fb52d74e6b8f7cb140a0b8ce7f9ec2e04e600789 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basin Battle <basin@battle>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:36:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Building previews move with you, never block you, and show as
 a light-blue ghost

A game object whose GAMEOBJECT_FLAGS carry 0x10000000 is a placement preview: a create of its
guid again moves it in place (with its new rotation and size) instead of leaving it where it
stood, a new look swaps in without the spawn fade, it builds no collision hull (so the hero never
walks into the station they are placing), and it neither fades in nor out (destroyed, it goes at
once). With 0x20000000 as well it draws as a ghost: half see-through and tinted light blue. An
unrigged model reads the tint from one palette slot the previews share, claimed once and never
skinned. Elwynn Survival's server sends the station being placed with both bits and the ring
under it with the first.
